    "result_text": "The test passes.\n\nI implemented \"task list per project, tickable\" as a full-stack additive change:\n\n**Database** \u2014 `V10__tasks.sql`: a new `tasks` table (`id`, `title`, `done` boolean, `project_id` FK).\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor) \u2014 new files only:\n- `Task` entity + `TaskRepository` (`findByProjectIdOrderByIdAsc`).\n- `ProjectTasksGet` \u2192 `GET /api/projects/{projectId}/tasks`.\n- `TaskToggle` \u2192 `POST /api/tasks/{id}/toggle` (flips `done`, records a `TASK_DONE`/`TASK_REOPENED` audit entry via the `Audit` service, 404 on unknown id).\n- Each wired by its own YAML under `rest/api/`.\n- Extended the (non-pinned) `TestSupportController` to seed `tasks` from the fixture ids and to `TRUNCATE ... RESTART IDENTITY` on reset.\n\n**Front-end** \u2014 additive, per the five rules:\n- New slot region `slots/defs/projectDetail.ts`, rendered once via `<ProjectDetail.Slot>` in the project detail route.\n- New `features/tasks/` \u2014 `queries.ts` (query key `['projects', id, 'tasks']`, toggle mutation), `ProjectTasksTable.tsx` (queries for itself, mutates + invalidates), and `tasks.slot.tsx` filling the region.\n\nIt matches the spec's `data-testid` contract exactly: `project-tasks-table`, `task-row-<id>`, `task-title`, `task-status` (`OPEN`/`DONE`), and `task-toggle-<id>`. Frontend typecheck and the Playwright test both pass.",
